{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$p=Get-Content docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml; foreach($n in 606,714,1698){$p[($n-1)..($n+12)]}; rg -n '\"'\"'^'\"\\\\[requirement.SR-(146|154|235)\\\\]' docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml; rg -n -A 4 'def test_tags_at_both_levels_union_and_a_repeat_is_clean' tests/test_gen_arch_map.py; rg -n 'TC-333|LLR-365|LLR-366|IF-263' docs/work/active/wi-997/WI-997-tag-this-repos-test-files.md\"","aggregated_output":"title = \"Prompts are reviewable files with a per-session audit trail\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-005\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-05\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"SECURITY\"]\r\nrequirement = \"Every prompt the delivered loop launches or an attended launcher renders as a review or critique brief shall be a shipped, reviewable file with strictly filled slots — listed by digest in a freshness-gated generated catalogue, each loop session recording which template it used and the fingerprint of what it rendered to.\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Prose steers the sessions this loop launches and had been reviewable only by reading Python source, which makes the process trusted rather than inspectable. The audit trail is the part that makes the move useful rather than cosmetic: without a per-session digest, \"which instruction did this session see\" stays an inference. (The argv-vs-shell-string transport decision is design, and lives one tier down in LLR-163.) C-SEC-5 requires that content composed for dispatch to an external model runner carry a DECLARED inclusion rule rather than an implicit one — a prompt assembled inside source is an unreviewed egress path no write-side gate covers, and shipping it as a reviewable file with a digest is what makes that rule readable.\"\"\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"\"\"An unknown or unfilled slot is a refusal and an attended render writes no brief; a missing shipped template is a named preflight refusal rather than a first-session crash; the catalogue lists every shipped prompt with its digest and `--check` fails when stale; a line-ending difference is not a digest change; an operator override is named in the session record rather than only in the launch flags.\"\"\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The need asks for prompts held to the same playbook as everything else; each prompt being a shipped file whose digest is catalogued, and each session recording the template it used, is that outcome, whatever the runner then does with the prompt.\"\"\"\r\naspect = \"process\"\r\n\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 1\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-007\"]\r\naspect = \"unattended-loop\"\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-155]\r\ntitle = \"Contested planning rounds for marked work\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-024\", \"SN-006\", \"SN-026\", \"SN-002\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-01\", \"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\r\nrequirement = \"\"\"Where work is declared as contested planning, the delivered loop content shall produce the selected decomposition through a bounded round of two independently authored rival plans — cross-critiqued, mechanically coverage-compared and arbitrated by fresh sessions — committing the selected outcome atomically as registry-valid queued rows and surfacing a non-converging round through the declared approval level, never falling back to a single uncontested plan silently.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"Realizes SN-024 (a decomposition judged by a competing plan and an independent arbiter rather than its author), with SN-026 (the planner pair prefers distinct families), SN-002 (the selected outcome lands as registry-valid rows, not prose) and SN-006. One row because the dual-plan round is one delivered capability with one observable outcome class (SELECT or PAGE); its state machine, briefs, adapters and isolation rules are the component tier's. Fan-out re-stamp: the round is one delivered capability with one observable outcome class, and its children are the successive phases of that single round — planner pair, briefs, coverage comparison, arbitration, isolation, disposition — none of which an adopter can obtain, refuse, or observe independently of the round, so the child count measures the round's step count rather than a merge of contracts.\"\r\nacceptance_criteria = \"For a recorded session of the claude, codex and opencode runners, the record carries the vocabulary's usage names and the revision they are pinned to; its input count includes cached input; its fresh input equals input less cache read and cache write; its raw usage reproduces the runner's usage events exactly; a count the runner does not report is empty, not zero; the route's provider column is filled from its roster row, the runner column is filled, and gen_ai.provider.name is anthropic for claude and openai for codex, also when that runner is reconfigured to another provider, and empty for opencode; a successful call's usage survives in the record even where the runner's result text is read from a separate file; and occupancy is the latest request's prompt over the model's window, blank where the runner reports no window, so no session reports occupancy above 100% because counts accumulated across its requests; and a session of any other runner, a stand-in included, carries the same columns, with its runner and its gen_ai.provider.name empty, and every count or raw usage the loop cannot read from the runner's output empty.\"\r\npriority = \"S\"\r\nverification = \"Test\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 6\r\nda_refs = [\"DA-016\"]\r\n\r\n[requirement.SR-227]\r\ntitle = \"Where the retention dial is on, adjudication routes retain sessions and reset them only when safe\"\r\nsn_refs = [\"SN-025\"]\r\nboundary_refs = [\"B-10\"]\r\nhat_refs = [\"PERFORMANCE\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\", \"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\"]\r\nrequirement = \"Where the declared adjudicator retention dial is above zero, the delivered adjudication content shall manage each retained-class adjudication consistently whether the coordinator or loop starts it: resume the route's active, unheld session in its model runner's resume form; mint and record a session id where the route has no active session; wait a bounded time where its active session is held, then run unretained and state why; record each call like any other; drain the session when its latest request's occupancy reaches the dial or the inputs it judges under change; retire it only when no work it has a stake in is pending, except that at the first keep after a blackout window it retires a session without a last use or last used before that window ended with reason blackout even when its chain is pending; retire it at once when a call fails except that an authentication failure records the failed call and leaves its session record unchanged; let no two calls use one retained session at once; write the retention state only whole, by one writer at a time; make any keep-warm call one bounded turn that never blocks the scheduler; compose both routes' retention request once; and, before retaining a family that uses a dedicated CLI home, read any long-lived credential at each launch from the location a declared environment setting names, keep every verbatim occurrence out of logs, records and commits, and refuse an absent or unreadable credential before launch, naming setup without interactive sign-in or fallback; and, where no long-lived credential applies, refuse either retained route when a dedicated-home reading is other than signed in before any launch, home creation, lease or retention-state write, naming the setup action without signing in automatically or falling back to a fresh session or another home.\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-025 asks that a configured agent implement toward the vision with no human curating what comes next; it does not name retaining a session, so this obligation arrives through three lenses rather than through the need's text. The performance lens listens for an operating-cost risk left unassessed: a run that spins a fresh adjudicator for every small work item reloads the spine on each call, and the usage record makes that cost visible, while resuming a session by id uses the provider's prompt cache. The unattended-operations lens listens for a silent degrade: a retained session that has filled, judges under changed rules, or is started in a home whose sign-in cannot be read degrades every later judgement with nothing paging anyone; a coordinator route that bypasses the retained operation repeats that cost and loses the state the loop preserves. One composition keeps both routes under the same drain and lease rules. The integrity lens listens for a durable artifact updated in place without an all-or-nothing guarantee and for a claim nothing can reclaim: two calls resuming one transcript at once corrupt it, so one call at a time holds a session, under a hold that expires when its holder is gone. Refusing an unreadable or absent sign-in before that hold prevents a failed retained launch from changing state or escaping into a person's default home. Retiring only when no work the session has a stake in is pending keeps a review, rework and re-review round trip in one session; a session is retained as a transcript a bounded process replays, never as a long-lived process, so an unattended run still cannot wait on a prompt. The dial is keyed off because turning it on is the owner's decision once the layer has been verified where it runs. Fed back to the need: SN-025's acceptance could name bounded operating cost per judgement as part of what lets a run proceed with no human curating it; until it does, this row is derived and says so.\"\"\"\r\n605:[requirement.SR-146]\n706:[requirement.SR-154]\n1820:[requirement.SR-235]\n1566:def test_tags_at_both_levels_union_and_a_repeat_is_clean(tmp_path):\n1567-    \"\"\"Implements: TC-404\"\"\"\n1568-    _write_tag_tree(tmp_path, {\"tests/test_levels.py\": TAG_LEVELS})\n1569-    node = \"tests/test_levels.py\"\n1570-    assert _tags_and_sites(tmp_path) == (\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
