{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n -A 8 '\"'^'\"\\\\[requirement.SR-(154|235)\\\\]' docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml; \"'$p=Get-Content tests/test_gen_arch_map.py; $p[1552..1580]; git diff --numstat fb2bb4e5aa87117e3caa53fff296e6d4c14161eb...68100ad8722f9a608067d01bb212c4b82c9253be -- project-trajectory/skills .agents/skills .claude/skills'","aggregated_output":"706:[requirement.SR-154]\n707-title = \"Independent review routed across families\"\n708-sn_refs = [\"SN-026\", \"SN-024\", \"SN-006\"]\n709-boundary_refs = [\"B-09\", \"B-10\"]\n710-hat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]\n711-requirement = \"The delivered loop content shall obtain, when unattended work reaches integration, each review or critique verdict the declared policy requires from a session that did not author the work — resolved per in-process phase and tier from the delivered agent registry's declared (family x model x tier) rows and only while the declared consent surface that turns managed selection on is present, drawn from a different model family wherever one is configured, degrading only to the documented same-family mode — with every selection logged before launch and a non-converging rework loop escalated through the declared approval level, and, where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, refuse build output at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when.\"\n712-rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions — every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, but only this row states the second opinion itself), SN-024 (an author cannot judge its own output) and SN-006. One row because routing, scheduling, scoring and escalation are one delivered contract — that the second opinion happens, independently, or its absence is documented — whose mechanics are the component details below it. The row also carries SN-026's DECLARATION and CONSENT half — `docs/agents.toml`'s pair-rows and the `docs/agents-enabled` surface whose presence turns managed selection on. That half had ZERO textual occurrence anywhere in the SR layer while `orphans=0` still held, because an orphan count proves a need has a citing row and never that the row carries the whole need. Managed selection is opt-in by consent rather than by configuration alone: a repository that declares families without dropping the surface has declared a capability, not turned one on, and the row now says so where a check can read it. fan-out re-stamp: the single plan's independent critique is one obligation carried by its briefs and filing and by its gate; the routing children remain separate.\"\"\"\n713-acceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review, or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, from a round the coordinator recorded as final for the lane's retained final reviewer, over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed. Where a claimed work item is marked for an in-lane single plan, no build output is accepted at its making or landing until a pass record binds its plan and Done-when; the plan either covers every Done-when item or excludes it with a reason, declares an architectural delta of none, or one carried within its scope. One revision receives a fresh independent critique. If that second critique does not read as an approval, only an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking or major finding permits the record; otherwise the item goes to the owner. A plan or Done-when changed after the record requires a fresh record. Ticking a Done-when item, or adding evidence to it, does not require a fresh record. Work items whose plan mark is absent, empty, none or dual are not held by this planning requirement; an unrecognized mark is held.\"\n714-priority = \"S\"\n--\n1820:[requirement.SR-235]\n1821-title = \"Attended independent review verdicts are recorded or refused\"\n1822-sn_refs = [\"SN-024\"]\n1823-boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\n1824-hat_refs = [\"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\"]\n1825-requirement = \"When an attended launcher submits an independent review verdict for a work item's lane, the delivered review content shall record a verdict bound to the reviewed commit in the review-round record form the delivered verdict reporting reads, or refuse a malformed or unbound verdict without a record.\"\n1826-rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-024 requires an independent critical eye and assigns the attended reviewer to the human, but does not require that verdict to survive as review history. The integrity-and-recoverability lens listens for a durable artifact updated without an all-or-nothing guarantee: accepting an unbound or malformed verdict can associate the wrong judgement with a lane, while dropping an accepted verdict leaves the next reader with no record of the independent review. A validated record-or-refusal boundary was chosen over treating submitted text as history because the latter cannot distinguish a verdict for the reviewed commit from unrelated text. Fed back to the need: SN-024's acceptance could name a durable attended-review record; until it does, this row is derived and says so.\"\n1827-acceptance_criteria = \"An attended verdict bound to the reviewed commit and carrying one complete verdict line whose declared finding count matches its finding lines is recorded as the next ordinal review-round record and appears in the review rollup; a verdict that is unbound, malformed or count-mismatched is refused with no record.\"\n1828-priority = \"S\"\n\r\n    Implements: TC-1\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_adds_its_own():\r\n    \"\"\"Own.\r\n\r\n    Implements: TC-2\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n'''\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_tags_at_both_levels_union_and_a_repeat_is_clean(tmp_path):\r\n    \"\"\"Implements: TC-404\"\"\"\r\n    _write_tag_tree(tmp_path, {\"tests/test_levels.py\": TAG_LEVELS})\r\n    node = \"tests/test_levels.py\"\r\n    assert _tags_and_sites(tmp_path) == (\r\n        {\r\n            \"TC-1\": [node, node + \"::test_repeats_its_module\"],\r\n            \"TC-2\": [node + \"::test_adds_its_own\"],\r\n        },\r\n        [],\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_a_non_python_test_file_is_read_at_file_level(tmp_path):\r\n    \"\"\"Implements: TC-404\"\"\"\r\n    _write_tag_tree(\r\n2\t2\t.agents/skills/byte-budget-guard/SKILL.md\n5\t3\t.agents/skills/coordinator-cycle/SKILL.md\n4\t0\t.agents/skills/coordinator-cycle/references/recipes.md\n10\t4\t.agents/skills/spine-authoring/references/in-lane.md\n2\t2\t.claude/skills/byte-budget-guard/SKILL.md\n5\t3\t.claude/skills/coordinator-cycle/SKILL.md\n4\t0\t.claude/skills/coordinator-cycle/references/recipes.md\n10\t4\t.claude/skills/spine-authoring/references/in-lane.md\n2\t2\tproject-trajectory/skills/byte-budget-guard/SKILL.md\n5\t3\tproject-trajectory/skills/coordinator-cycle/SKILL.md